I have been following this discussion with interest, but there is one thing
I don't understand. When you say you have informed the University that a
particular poster is making defamatory postings how do you expect the
University to judge whether that is indeed the case? That is, there is
clearly a disagreement over a particular statement, and you are asking the
University (or other service provider) to decide that you are correct in the
absence of any evidence either way. If this were to be applied by service
providers it could lead to the situation whereby anyone disagreeing with
statements, articles, or a particular poster, could inform the provider and
insist that they stop that poster from continuing to post. This I feel would
have a harmful affect on the freedom of discussion on Usenet and other
network media. 

